# Shell scripts must keep LF endings, always.
#
# This repo is edited on Windows, where git's autocrlf hands out CRLF on
# checkout. A shell script with CRLF fails on macOS and Linux with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" — an error that names the interpreter
# rather than the line endings, and so reads as a broken Python or a
# broken Mac rather than a whitespace problem. It has cost people whole
# afternoons. Pinning the endings here removes the possibility.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.command   text eol=lf
